**Role Summary**  

Reporting to the Asset Manager, the Analyst / Senior Analyst, Asset Management plays a key role in supporting and driving the financial and operational performance of the industrial real estate portfolio.  

This role will be filled at either the Analyst or Senior Analyst level depending on the successful candidate’s experience and qualifications.  

At the Analyst level, this is an entry\-level opportunity into industrial real estate, focused on supporting operational and financial reporting, budgeting, valuations, and transaction\-related analysis. At the Senior Analyst level, the role carries increased responsibility for leading financial analysis, asset planning, valuations, and providing strategic insight to support leasing, development, acquisition, disposition, and financing activities. The Senior Analyst also acts as a trusted analytical partner to Asset Managers and senior leadership and provides informal mentorship to junior team members. **Core Responsibilities**

* Assist with or lead the preparation and analysis of asset plans, and annual operating and capital budgets in accordance with portfolio and asset strategies;
* Provide lease deal analysis on prospective lease transactions, including financial, cash flow, and credit analysis of prospective tenants (with increased complexity and scenario analysis at the Senior Analyst level);
* Prepare, analyze, and interpret operational and financial data for strategic review by Asset Managers and executives, providing insights and recommendations as appropriate;
* Provide analytical support for development\-related activities, including feasibility analysis, pro forma modeling, and return analysis;
* Assist with or lead the preparation, review, and analysis of monthly, quarterly, and annual reporting, ensuring accuracy, consistency, and clarity for internal and external stakeholders;
* Fully analyze consolidated portfolio financial results and organize materials for quarterly reports, investor presentations, and other stakeholder reporting as required;
* Coordinate with Property Management and Leasing teams to prepare weekly reports, move\-out reports, and other operational summaries;
* Assist with or lead the quarterly and annual investment property valuation processes, including the development, maintenance, and review of Argus models;
* Support property acquisitions, dispositions, and financing initiatives through underwriting, due diligence analysis, financial modeling, and presentation materials;
* Develop and maintain knowledge of industrial real estate market trends, leasing activity, and capital markets across Canada through research and broker relationships;
* Support Asset Management team members and senior leadership with ad\-hoc analytical requests and strategic initiatives;
* At the Senior Analyst level, provide guidance and informal mentorship to junior analysts, promoting best practices in financial modeling, analysis, and reporting.
 **Required Skills and Experience**

*For Analyst, Asset Management:*

* Undergraduate degree in Finance, Business Administration, Urban Planning, Real Estate, or a related field;
* Less than one year of relevant work experience or co\-op/internship experience in real estate, finance, or a related analytical role;
* Strong financial and analytical skills with a clear interest in real estate operations and investments;
* Advanced knowledge of Excel and PowerPoint; familiarity with accounting and reporting systems is an asset;
* Exceptional attention to detail with strong organizational skills;
* Ability to think logically, problem solve effectively, and work efficiently under pressure;
* Excellent written and verbal communication skills;
* Results\-oriented, curious, collaborative, and approachable.

 *For Senior Analyst, Asset Management:*

